Application Process\nReady to Apply?\nComplete LSU New Orleans Online Application\nFollow instructions for Graduate Applicants\nComplete all required sections, upload required documents, and pay application fee.\nM.S. Biological Sciences 1-Year Non-thesis Option\nAdmission Requirements\nGPA of 3.0 is preferred\n1 letter of recommendation from a professor familiar with your academic potential\nOnline Application Form\nNext Steps\nDegree Requirements (M.S.)\nDegree Requirements (Ph.D.)\nHow to Apply\nFinancial Support\nAdvising\nDue Dates\nFall applications are accepted until July 1\nSpring applications are accepted through November 1\nM.S. Biological Sciences Thesis Option and\nPh.D. Integrative Biology\nAdmission Requirements\nA baccalaureate degree from an accredited university or college.\nA grade point average of at least 3.0 (on a 4.0 scale).\nFor international applicants whose native language is not English, satisfactory scores on the TOEFL, IELTS, or PTE, or successful completion of the IELP program at LSU New Orleans. Please see current requirements.\nSatisfactory academic standing at the last university or college attended.\nApplication Requirements\nThree letters of recommendation\nClear Statement of Purpose of your research interest, experiences, and goals\nPrevious research experience is desired\nDeadlines and Funding\nFor fall admission, the review of applicants begins on February 1 and continues until all positions are filled. For spring admission, applications must be received by October 1. Applications received after these deadlines may be considered depending upon availability of positions and funding.\nThe Department strives to support all students admitted into the MS and PhD program by teaching assistantships, research assistantships, scholarships, or fellowships. Learn more.\nWhen considering applicants for admission, the Graduate Committee will consider the student's academic record, test scores, research experience, letters of recommendation, and potential to successfully complete a research project in this department.\nFooter\nContact\n2000 Lakeshore Drive New Orleans, LA 70148\n[email protected]\n[email protected]\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (504) 384-7924\n+1 (504) 384-7924\nLearn\nAdmission information\nPrograms of study\nScholarships and awards\nTuition and fees\nGraduate programs\nFinancial aid\nImportant dates & deadlines\nExperience\nInternational center\nOur campus\nStudent life\nHousing\nCareer services\nAlumni\nMake a gift\nAnnual Security Report\nConnect\nAll social\nUniversity calendar\nNews\nFor parents\nEspanol - Tieng Viet\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nNon-Discrimination\nTitle IX\nCampus Crime\nEmergency Preparedness\n\u00a9 2026 LSU New Orleans. All Rights Reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics/cos/biology/graduate/application-process#main"], ["", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/"], ["", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions"], ["Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions"], ["Undergraduate Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/apply-freshman"], ["Transfer Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/transfer"], ["Adult Learners", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/adult-learners"], ["Military Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/military-veteran"], ["Graduate Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/graduate"], ["International Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics/grad/admission-requirements/international"], ["Explore Majors", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics#majors"], ["Graduate Programs", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics/grad/programs"], ["Apply", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/apply"], ["Important Dates & Deadlines", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/deadlines"], ["Tuition & Fees", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions/tuition-fees"], ["Accepted Students", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu